{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "radiation-biology",
    "title": "Radiation Biology",
    "order": 7
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "tolerance-dose",
    "title": "Tolerance Dose",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Threshold and Tolerance Dose",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "threshold dose",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is the dose below which no biological response is observed; above it, a response appears. "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Tolerance dose",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " describes the dose at which a normal tissue can be irradiated with an acceptable, defined risk of significant complications \u2014 it's inherently a statement about risk, not a hard line between \"safe\" and \"unsafe.\""
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "TD5/5 and TD50/5",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "TD5/5 (minimum tolerance dose):",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " the dose expected to result in a 5% risk of severe complications within 5 years of irradiation."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "TD50/5 (maximum tolerance dose):",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " the dose expected to result in a 50% risk of severe complications within 5 years."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Example TD5/5 values: whole lens of the eye ~10 Gy, whole brain ~45 Gy, whole lung ~17.5 Gy. Every organ has its own characteristic tolerance, which is exactly why treatment planning constrains dose to specific organs at risk differently depending on which organ is nearby."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A dose expected to cause severe complications in 50% of patients within 5 years is called:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "TD5/5",
              "TD50/5"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "TD50/5 is the dose associated with a 50% complication risk within 5 years \u2014 the \"maximum tolerance dose.\""
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Therapeutic Ratio",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "therapeutic ratio",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " compares the dose that controls the tumor against the dose that damages normal tissue:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Therapeutic Ratio = Normal Tissue Tolerance Dose (NTTD) / Tumor Lethal Dose (TLD)",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "favorable",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " therapeutic ratio means the tumor lethal dose occurs at a lower dose than the normal tissue tolerance dose \u2014 you can deliver a tumor-killing dose without exceeding what nearby normal tissue can tolerate. An "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "unfavorable",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " ratio means the reverse: normal tissue tolerance is reached before the tumor lethal dose, forcing compromises in the treatment plan."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Dose-Response Curve Shapes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Three basic dose-response relationship shapes describe how biological effects relate to dose:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Type"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Shape"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Meaning"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Linear, nonthreshold",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Straight line through the origin"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Any dose, however small, carries some risk of effect \u2014 this is the basis for radiation protection dose limits"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Linear, threshold",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Straight line, but starting from a nonzero dose"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "No response below a certain dose; above it, response rises linearly"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Nonlinear, threshold",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Curved, starting from a nonzero dose"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "No response below threshold; above it, response follows a nonlinear (often S-shaped) curve"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation protection guides are deliberately based on the most conservative assumption: a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "linear, nonthreshold",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " relationship for stochastic effects like radiation-induced cancer."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Deterministic vs. Stochastic Effects",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Deterministic (nonstochastic) effects",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " have a threshold and increase in "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "severity",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " with dose above that threshold. Skin erythema, cataracts, and hair loss are examples \u2014 and these follow a threshold dose-response curve."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Stochastic effects",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " have no established threshold, and increasing dose increases the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "probability",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " of the effect occurring, not its severity. Radiation-induced cancer and genetic effects are the principal examples, and these follow the linear, nonthreshold model."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation-induced cataracts, which worsen with higher dose above a threshold, are an example of:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "A stochastic effect",
              "A deterministic (nonstochastic) effect"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A threshold effect that increases in severity with dose is deterministic, not stochastic."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Normal Organ Tissue Tolerances in Practice",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment planning constrains dose to organs at risk based on published tolerance data. This is why a plan for a brain tumor near the optic apparatus, or a lung tumor near the spinal cord, is built around specific numeric dose-volume limits for those structures \u2014 not just \"as low as possible,\" but a defined, evidence-based tolerance threshold weighed against the dose needed for tumor control."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered threshold and tolerance dose, TD5/5 and TD50/5, the therapeutic ratio (favorable vs. unfavorable), the three dose-response curve shapes, and the deterministic vs. stochastic effect distinction."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This lesson is the conceptual bridge between Cell Survival Curves (what happens at the cellular level) and the Radiation Effects lesson (what happens at the whole-organ and whole-body level)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "import_notes": [
